**Findings**
1. High: the public presenter kept restart-specific messaging visible even after recovery had completed, which leaked recovery semantics beyond the active recovery window and conflicted with AC1/AC2. Fixed in [dashboard-presenter.js](/home/codexuser/bmad-6-workshop/src/features/dashboard/presenters/dashboard-presenter.js#L67) so restart copy only appears while `recovery.phase === "recovering"`. Coverage added in [dashboard.presenter.test.mjs](/home/codexuser/bmad-6-workshop/tests/unit/dashboard.presenter.test.mjs#L266).

2. Medium: the persisted recovery artifact contradicted the checked-in live snapshot state, still reporting `recovering` after the newer live snapshot had resumed. Fixed in [dashboard-recovery.json](/home/codexuser/bmad-6-workshop/runtime/snapshots/dashboard-recovery.json#L1) so the stored recovery state now matches the resumed live publish.

The workflow is complete. Story status is now `done` in [3-5-recover-the-display-after-interruption-or-restart.md](/home/codexuser/bmad-6-workshop/docs/sprint-artifacts/3-5-recover-the-display-after-interruption-or-restart.md#L3) and [sprint-status.yaml](/home/codexuser/bmad-6-workshop/docs/sprint-artifacts/sprint-status.yaml#L27). `npm run validate` passed.
